# Machine-specific Fish configuration
# Copy this file to ~/.config/fish/config.local.fish and update with your settings
# This file is NOT tracked in git - it's specific to each machine
#
# config.fish sources this last, so anything here overrides conf.d/.
# It is sourced for non-interactive shells too, which is deliberate: env vars
# set here need to reach scripts. Interactive-only things (abbreviations,
# colours, prompt tweaks) should say so, the way conf.d/30-interactive.fish
# does -- otherwise every `fish -c` pays for them.

# Example: Work-specific environment variables
# set -gx WORK_PROXY "proxy.example.com:8080"
# set -gx CUSTOM_PATH "/opt/custom/bin"

# Example: interactive-only settings
# if status is-interactive
#     abbr work 'cd ~/work-projects'
# end

# Add any other machine-specific environment variables, abbreviations, or functions here
